ull,"closed_at":null},"comments":2,"created_at":"2024-10-15T12:02:05Z","updated_at":"2024-10-15T19:07:06Z","closed_at":"2024-10-15T19:07:05Z","author_association":"MEMBER","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Discussed in https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/discussions/12001\r\n\r\n<div type='discussions-op-text'>\r\n\r\n<sup>Originally posted by **rad-pat** October 15, 2024</sup>\r\nWhen trying to upgrade to 2.0.35 from 1.4.54, we cannot because we get a pickling error in 2.0.35. \r\n\r\nI'm sure pickling queries is not the best way to transport between app layers, however it is currently being done in our app until I can update it. \r\n\r\nWe have a couple of custom types to control behaviour across dialects where certain types are not yet supported. It's possible that some of them are not needed any longer. However, here is a very quick example of the pickling error in case it is something easy to address.\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport pickle\r\nimport sqlalchemy as sa\r\n\r\nclass MyType(sa.TypeDecorator):\r\n    impl = sa.NVARCHAR\r\n    cache_ok = True\r\n\r\n    def load_dialect_impl(self, dialect):\r\n        if dialect.name in {'postgresql'}:\r\n            return dialect.type_descriptor(sa.UnicodeText)\r\n        else:\r\n            return self.impl\r\n\r\nm = sa.MetaData()\r\nt = sa.Table('test', m, sa.Column('id', MyType))\r\n\r\ndelete_query = sa.delete(t).where(t.c.id == '1')\r\n\r\np = pickle.dumps(delete_query)\r\n\r\n#    p = pickle.dumps(delete_query)\r\n#        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n#_pickle.PicklingError: Can't pickle <class 'sqlalchemy.sql.type_api.TDComparator'>: attribute lookup TDComparator on sqlalchemy.sql.type_api failed\r\n```</div>","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/12002/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/12002/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}